Usage: time [OPTION]... COMMAND [ARG]...

Run a command and report how long it took.

The command is executed as a child process and the child exit status is
returned unchanged. Timing data is written to standard error.

With -p, print POSIX-compatible timing lines.

OPTIONS:
  -p, --posix    report timing in POSIX format
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
